  "notes": [
    "Each runtime .tscn owns its editor-visible Terrain, collision bodies, and room markers directly; no separate terrain scene or code-generated map is used.",
    "scenes/regions/ash_forest.tscn is the A2 region entry scene to the R01 runtime scene. A1 north gate routes directly to R01.",
    "R01->R04 drop trigger uses the narrow shaft Marker2D (672,780), width 48 and height 120 so a committed fall enters R04 while a clean jump can cross; R03->R04 uses Marker2D (425,675), width 150 and height 220. H02 is placed on the R04 crypt landing (90,380) and returns to R04 EntryH02Return (350,380).",
    "C03 (R06/A3) and H02 (R04/H02) forward and return destinations were statically checked against the owning room runtime and Marker2D spawn anchors; still pending Godot 4.6.1 playtesting.",
    "A2 room transitions preserve a valid A2 checkpoint; incoming spawn side is saved before the transient side is reset. Death recovery accepts only the six known A2 room IDs.",
    "Cross-region returns are room-specific: the active C03/H02 route definitions directly target R06/EntryC03Return and R04/EntryH02Return. R05 remains an internal A2 room and has no cross-region return marker.",
    "All connection status values remain implemented_pending_godot_playtest until the user verifies physical collision and scene transitions in Godot 4.6.1.",
    "A2 side boundary walls now scale to each room's room_height (-100px to room_height+100px); the A5 assembled-region wall sizing remains unchanged."
  ],
